# Stable device identity for the CS7.1 controller adapter.
#
# Matches on USB vendor ID, product ID *and* serial number - not vendor/product
# alone - so this rule cannot pick up a different adapter of the same model,
# and does not match every generic USB-serial device on the bus. No adapter
# has been approved yet (docs/architecture/deployment-and-operations.md); the
# three placeholders below are substituted by install.sh from values the
# installing technician records as hardware evidence, per PI-HIL-001. This
# file as checked in matches nothing until that substitution happens.
#
# The symlink's group and mode are the actual access control: cs71d is the
# only account ever placed in the cs71d group, so only it can open the real
# device node this resolves to. TAG+="systemd" plus SYSTEMD_WANTS asks systemd
# to start cs71d.service the moment the adapter is present, rather than
# leaving that to boot-time unit ordering against a path that may not exist
# yet.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="@@VENDOR_ID@@", ATTRS{idProduct}=="@@PRODUCT_ID@@", ATTRS{serial}=="@@SERIAL@@", SYMLINK+="cs71", GROUP="cs71d", MODE="0660", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}="cs71d.service"
